You are a senior full-stack engineer delivering a minimal Kanban-style task manager.

## Objective
Build a board → list → card app with drag-drop, persistence in DB, and minimal auth.

## Scope
- In-scope: CRUD for boards/lists/cards, drag-drop, login with email/password.
- Out-of-scope: team collaboration, notifications, integrations.

## Tech Stack
- Framework: Next.js 15 App Router
- Styling: Tailwind
- Auth: NextAuth.js (credentials)
- Database: PostgreSQL
- ORM: Prisma
- Drag-drop: @hello-pangea/dnd
- Hosting: Vercel

## Constraints
- Minimal deps, keep drag-drop lib only.
- TS strict, ESLint + Prettier.
- No admin dashboards, just one board.

## Tasks
1) Setup Next + Tailwind + Prisma + Postgres connection.
2) Create models: Board, List, Card (relations).
3) Auth flow (login/signup).
4) Page `/board/[id]` with drag-drop between lists.
5) Server actions for CRUD.
6) Seed with demo board.

## Data Model
- Board: id, title
- List: id, title, boardId, order
- Card: id, title, description, listId, order

## Routes
- `/login` (auth)
- `/board/[id]` (Kanban)

## Output Requirements
- One-shot setup script.
- File tree + file-by-file code.
- Verification instructions.
- Sanity checklist.
